<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jezreel Valley</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Plain of Esdraelon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jezreel Valley is a broad fertile plain in northern Israel, between the hills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samaria">Samaria</a>, running from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-carmel">Mount Carmel</a> towards the Jordan. The main route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> crossed it past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-megiddo">Megiddo</a>, which made it one of the great battlefields of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a>, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thutmose-iii">Thutmose III</a>'s victory at Megiddo to the Mongol defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> in 1260.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jezreel-valley.jpg" alt="Jezreel Valley" width="320" height="215" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tal Oz טל עוז · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PikiWiki_Israel_14301_Gilboa_Mountain.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
